Plus One | Carry Simulation | O(n) Java

## Intuition

When adding 1, only the digits from right to left are affected. If a digit is less than 9, increment it and return immediately. Otherwise, it becomes 0 and the carry moves to the previous digit.

## Approach

1. Traverse the array from right to left.
2. If the current digit is less than 9, increment it and return the array.
3. Otherwise, set it to 0 and continue propagating the carry.
4. If the loop finishes, all digits were 9. Create a new array of size n + 1, set the first element to 1, and return it. In Java, the remaining elements are automatically initialized to 0.

## Complexity

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(1) auxiliary space.
A new array of size n + 1 is created only when all digits are 9, making the worst-case space complexity O(n).

## Code

class Solution {
public int[] plusOne(int[] digits) {
int n = digits.length;

```
    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        if (digits[i] < 9) {
            digits[i]++;
            return digits;
        }
        digits[i] = 0;
    }

    int[] arr = new int[n + 1];
    arr[0] = 1;
    return arr;
}
```

}
